# Deploy-only Dockerfile. Coolify builds THIS on the VPS; the real build
# happens on a GitHub runner (see .github/workflows/build-image.yml).
#
# Why the indirection: Coolify cannot convert an existing git-backed
# application to its "Docker Image" type — the API rejects that build pack, and
# recreating the app would mean rebuilding 26 environment variables, the
# persistent volume, the domains and the Traefik labels by hand. So the app
# stays on the "dockerfile" build pack and this file makes that build a no-op:
# a single FROM that resolves to the already-built image. Pull and retag only,
# no compile, so the OOM that broke deploys for three weeks cannot recur here.
#
# IMAGE_REF is supplied by Coolify as a build arg from the application's
# build-time environment variable of the same name. The workflow sets it to the
# immutable sha-<commit> tag before triggering a deploy, which guarantees the
# VPS pulls that exact image instead of reusing a stale local copy of a moving
# tag. The :main default only applies to a manual deploy triggered from the
# Coolify UI.
ARG IMAGE_REF=ghcr.io/byteprima/archer-infotech:main
FROM ${IMAGE_REF}
